      "comment": "Message recovery, the only thing this protocol has where FIX has a ResendRequest. 7000 names a stream in the header's AlphaChar and a cursor in SequenceNumber (9492); the answer is HEADER_RECORD (7011), a MESSAGE_RECORD (7021) per message after that cursor, and TRAILER_RECORD (7031). 9405 is the header's TimeStamp1, which IS that cursor -- so the download resumes from a value the venue assigned, which is why this captures it rather than hard-coding one. Without that, the scenario would replay the whole daemon's history on its second run in the same process and assert against a moving target."
    },
